{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_87ca730efa1d9fe6ab0bcd3f89805a1b759f4929b8fdd78256393e0629272474"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"requirements.txt pins openai, anthropic, playwright, flask, fastapi, uvicorn, pydantic, PyJWT, psycopg, and pytest-based test dependencies, among others."}],"claim_ids":["clm_87ca730efa1d9fe6ab0bcd3f89805a1b759f4929b8fdd78256393e0629272474"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:51:28Z","created_by_operation":"op_6703a04bdc4f40cc88801baf7c3f0d28","id":"pg_da853f8769465d4789d29e3070238ed6","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/firetix-vibe-coding-penetration-tester-requirements-txt-2625ff0bc570-9e3070238ed6.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_98ea06f052425155a5b79383a3433dd8"],"title":"firetix/vibe-coding-penetration-tester/requirements.txt @ 2625ff0bc570","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:51:28Z","updated_by_operation":"op_6703a04bdc4f40cc88801baf7c3f0d28"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_0707f126ddaecea3908de8cce39a5b9d9b743e28a547e1e5dde62cf52a7aa2fe"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Optional hosted/billing endpoints include GET /api/entitlements, POST /api/billing/checkout, and POST /api/billing/webhook, plus a mock checkout route for local/test setups."},{"claim_ids":["clm_0e5c65a5f83a2f8f61e998d1dc8051d28918a78f9111e0b7711ba0aae5150e8c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The modular web app exposes session, scan, activity, logs, and report endpoints such as POST /api/scan/start, POST /api/scan/cancel, and GET /api/report/<report_id>."},{"claim_ids":["clm_139af722d641765e06102a34b79f07fcbd173fd9e1f336b8fe2cf4e055c645e9"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The tool requires at least one LLM provider: an OpenAI API key, an Anthropic API key, or an Ollama server (default localhost:11434)."},{"claim_ids":["clm_4354df2c66fca2a8a051be85864e2fc8b18947e1e5550c73beedabeb8b226ee0"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The tool is restricted by its own notice to targets the user owns or has explicit authorization to test; unauthorized scanning may violate law and policy."},{"claim_ids":["clm_626a316d06dbb7623bb1e571087a3af8450e71dc2cc21e998b84bd7b3801d1a2"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The repository includes a CLI entrypoint (main.py), modular Flask web API (run_web.py, web_api/), a legacy web_ui.py, agents/, tools/, and sample reports directories."},{"claim_ids":["clm_679ef622b467298283b7c8bb9e00843c131bb668c3c01447ac8d229363a45304"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Scanning is scope-aware with three scope modes: url, domain, and subdomain."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6f460a68f770910367b48ae7e4e9f815391d8b7a7b9b45bd3e2fa149886465d2"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The tool coordinates specialized security agents to discover and validate common web vulnerabilities and generates reproducible Markdown and JSON reports."},{"claim_ids":["clm_709d309b198df576f606e6af6f740b58aead3524c8d51bfaa114081ac1011434"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: tests are run via ./run_tests.sh or focused pytest suites (unit, integration, API E2E, frontend E2E, Vercel preview) with markers defined in pytest.ini."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8f51319fe06d48e12e29f488bae3973f72bbab7ae627bbfd60afe833ce4cb0c3"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The CLI accepts --url (required), --model (default gpt-5.2), --provider (openai/anthropic/ollama), --scope, --output, --verbose, and --ollama-url options."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a96814219c2c3881607dc4a6d540fffa933bdb3c6484f45011dbcc4af020bc12"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A multi-agent scan workflow covers discovery, planning, and vulnerability testing, with browser automation via Playwright for realistic interaction testing."}],"claim_ids":["clm_0707f126ddaecea3908de8cce39a5b9d9b743e28a547e1e5dde62cf52a7aa2fe","clm_0e5c65a5f83a2f8f61e998d1dc8051d28918a78f9111e0b7711ba0aae5150e8c","clm_139af722d641765e06102a34b79f07fcbd173fd9e1f336b8fe2cf4e055c645e9","clm_4354df2c66fca2a8a051be85864e2fc8b18947e1e5550c73beedabeb8b226ee0","clm_626a316d06dbb7623bb1e571087a3af8450e71dc2cc21e998b84bd7b3801d1a2","clm_679ef622b467298283b7c8bb9e00843c131bb668c3c01447ac8d229363a45304","clm_6f460a68f770910367b48ae7e4e9f815391d8b7a7b9b45bd3e2fa149886465d2","clm_709d309b198df576f606e6af6f740b58aead3524c8d51bfaa114081ac1011434","clm_8f51319fe06d48e12e29f488bae3973f72bbab7ae627bbfd60afe833ce4cb0c3","clm_a96814219c2c3881607dc4a6d540fffa933bdb3c6484f45011dbcc4af020bc12"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:51:28Z","created_by_operation":"op_6703a04bdc4f40cc88801baf7c3f0d28","id":"pg_da8c95e7ddde5aa8aefe929e02aaa77b","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/firetix-vibe-coding-penetration-tester-readme-md-2625ff0bc570-929e02aaa77b.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_f1ff546ea227596882f7f4dce678ca93"],"title":"firetix/vibe-coding-penetration-tester/README.md @ 2625ff0bc570","updated_at":"